</code></pre> <p>So the caller's entire <code>Cookie</code> header is copied three ways:</p> <ol> <li><code>exportSession=&lt;value of presenton_session&gt;</code> in the query string (<code>extractSessionTokenFromCookieHeader()</code> uses the regex <code>/(?:^|;\s*)presenton_session=([^;]+)/</code>, <code>servers/nextjs/lib/run-bundled-presentation-export.ts:27-38</code>).</li> <li><code>#exportCookie=&lt;whole cookie header&gt;</code> in the URL fragment.</li> <li><code>cookieHeader</code> in the task, which the runner turns into <code>urlConfigs</code> cookies for the page origin.</li> </ol> <p>If the incoming request had no cookie, <code>desktopCookieHeader()</code> supplies <code>presenton_desktop_session=&lt;token&gt;</code> in Electron mode (<code>servers/nextjs/lib/run-bundled-presentation-export.ts:154</code>, <code>servers/nextjs/lib/desktop-auth.ts:7-12</code>).</p> <p>Gotcha: the session JWT is in a query string</p> <p><code>exportSession</code> puts the user's 30-day session JWT (<code>SESSION_TTL_SECONDS</code>, <code>servers/fastapi/api/v1/auth/config.py:12</code>) into the request line of <code>GET /pdf-maker</code>. In Docker that request goes through nginx, and <code>nginx.conf</code> does not configure <code>access_log</code>, so nginx's default access logging applies to it. The fragment (<code>#exportCookie=...</code>) is never sent to any server, which is why FastAPI's own logging strips everything after <code>#</code> (<code>servers/fastapi/services/export_task_service.py:430</code>). Treat access logs on a Presenton host as sensitive.</p>

Endpoint Exports Code <code>POST /api/v1/ppt/presentation/{id}/export</code> with body <code>{"export_as": "pptx"}</code> an existing deck, without regenerating <code>servers/fastapi/api/v1/ppt/endpoints/presentation.py:1642-1678</code> <code>POST /api/v1/ppt/presentation/generate</code> the newly generated deck (step 9 of the handler) <code>servers/fastapi/api/v1/ppt/endpoints/presentation.py:3098-3104</code>, <code>3169-3190</code> <code>POST /api/v1/ppt/presentation/generate/async</code> same, in a background task; <code>path</code> and <code>edit_path</code> are stored in the task's <code>data</code> <code>servers/fastapi/api/v1/ppt/endpoints/presentation.py:3125-3126</code>, <code>3240-3271</code> <code>POST /api/v1/ppt/presentation/edit</code> the edited deck <code>servers/fastapi/api/v1/ppt/endpoints/presentation.py:3339-3344</code> <code>POST /api/v1/ppt/presentation/derive</code> a copied and edited deck <code>servers/fastapi/api/v1/ppt/endpoints/presentation.py:3383-3388</code> v2 smart generation (sync and async) the smart deck after its SSE stream completes <code>servers/fastapi/api/v2/ppt/endpoints/presentation.py:139-149</code> <p><code>export_as</code> defaults to <code>pptx</code> everywhere (<code>servers/fastapi/models/generate_presentation_request.py:41</code>, <code>64</code>, <code>servers/fastapi/models/presentation_from_template.py:14</code>, and the <code>Body(embed=True)</code> default at <code>servers/fastapi/api/v1/ppt/endpoints/presentation.py:1646</code>). The response model is <code>PresentationPathAndEditPath</code> (<code>servers/fastapi/models/presentation_and_path.py:5-11</code>):</p> <pre><code>{
